# Host configuration for a NazaréNow deployment.
#
# Copy to /etc/nazarenow/nazarenow.env on the host, edit, and keep it there. It is read by
# every unit in deploy/systemd/, so the API, the scheduler and the backup timer cannot end
# up disagreeing about where the store is — which is the failure ADR 0005 warns about, and
# which presents as "no conditions have been ingested yet" beside a perfectly good database.
#
# This file is the example. The real one never enters the repository.
#   sudo install -d -m 750 -o nazarenow -g nazarenow /etc/nazarenow
#   sudo install -m 640 -o root -g nazarenow deploy/nazarenow.env.example /etc/nazarenow/nazarenow.env

# --- The store ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# ADR 0007 names this file as the one asset whose loss costs the project every accuracy
# claim it will ever make, so where it sits is not an afterthought. `/var/lib` is where state
# a service owns belongs, and on the current host it is also on the SSD, because the SSD is
# the root filesystem. On a Pi that boots from an SD card this must be moved onto real
# storage instead: a Pipeline Run writes every three hours forever and a card's write
# endurance is finite.
#
# `store.py` anchors its default path to the repository, which is right for a source
# checkout and wrong for an installed package — the anchor would land beside the
# virtualenv. A packaged deployment must set this explicitly.
NAZARENOW_DB=/var/lib/nazarenow/nazarenow.db

# --- Backups -----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Where `backup-store.sh` writes its snapshots. Beside the store by default, which protects
# against corruption of the live file but NOT against losing the machine — that is what
# NAZARENOW_BACKUP_REMOTE below is for, and why leaving it empty fails ADR 0007's criterion.
NAZARENOW_BACKUP_DIR=/var/lib/nazarenow/backups

# Retention, grandfather-father-son. The newest snapshot in each day, week and month is
# kept while that bucket has budget left, and a snapshot kept as a daily also occupies its
# week's and its month's slot — so the buckets nest rather than multiply. A year of daily
# backups collapses to about twenty snapshots reaching back twelve months, instead of thirty
# near-identical copies of the last month.
#
# Worth knowing what this does and does not fix: it bounds what is *stored*. A full snapshot
# is still uploaded every night, because each one is an independent gzip of the whole store.
# If that upload volume ever becomes the problem, the answer is a deduplicating backup tool
# (restic, borg), not a smaller number here.
NAZARENOW_KEEP_DAILY=7
NAZARENOW_KEEP_WEEKLY=4
NAZARENOW_KEEP_MONTHLY=12

# An rclone remote, as `remote:path`. Leave empty and backups stay on the host — which
# ADR 0007's criterion explicitly does not accept, because a snapshot on the same SSD as
# the original dies with it. Set it and every snapshot is copied off the machine.
#   rclone config            # once, interactively, to create the remote
NAZARENOW_BACKUP_REMOTE=
